paragraphs.en:
1. A method for purifying a tembotrione product, the method comprising the following steps:
1) dissolving the tembotrione product in an aqueous solution and raising the temperature;
2) adding an adsorbent, then holding the temperature and carrying out hot filtration;
3) adjusting, under temperature control, the pH of the aqueous solution to below 3, then cooling and crystallising the purified tembotrione out of the solution;
the aqueous solution referred to in step 1) is a solution obtained by mixing acetonitrile, methanol, ethanol, dimethylformamide with water;
the water content of the aqueous solution is 20%-40%; the said raising of the temperature is raising the temperature to 30 C-60 C;
the holding time referred to in step 2) is 0.2 h-1 h;
the adsorbent is activated carbon or diatomaceous earth.
